<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 4 March, from 581 to 1966.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">581 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,445 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yang Jian proclaims himself Emperor Wen of Sui</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui">Yang Jian</a>, an official of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a>, seized power and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> as Emperor Wen. In 589 he conquered the southern Chen dynasty, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after nearly three centuries of division.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui">Emperor Wen of Sui</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1152">1152 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">874 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick Barbarossa elected King of Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The German princes chose Frederick of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> as king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>. Crowned emperor in 1155, he fought repeated campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and clashed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> until his death on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> in 1190.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1238">1238 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">788 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mongols destroy the army of Vladimir on the Sit River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Sit, a tributary of the Mologa, the Mongol army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a> surprised and destroyed the forces of Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-of-vladimir">Yuri II of Vladimir</a>, who was killed. The defeat ended organised resistance in north-eastern Rus'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sit-river">Battle of the Sit River</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1461">1461 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">565 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward IV proclaimed King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Yorkist Edward, Earl of March, was proclaimed king in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, deposing the Lancastrian Henry VI. Weeks later he won the bloody Battle of Towton, securing his throne.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Constitution takes effect as the first Congress meets</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The new federal government began operation as Congress gathered at Federal Hall in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, though it took weeks to reach a quorum. The Constitution is the oldest written national constitution still in force.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln inaugurated as 16th President</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With seven states already seceded, Lincoln appealed to 'the better angels of our nature' in his inaugural address. War began at Fort Sumter five weeks later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tchaikovsky's 'Swan Lake' premieres at the Bolshoi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first production in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> was poorly received. Revived in St Petersburg in 1895 with choreography by Petipa and Ivanov, it became the most famous of all ballets.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Franklin D. Roosevelt inaugurated in the depths of the Depression</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With banks failing nationwide, Roosevelt told Americans 'the only thing we have to fear is fear itself'. In his first hundred days Congress passed a wave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-deal">New Deal</a> legislation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon says the Beatles are 'more popular than Jesus'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The remark appeared in an interview in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>'s Evening Standard and passed unnoticed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Reprinted in the US months later, it led to record burnings and radio bans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 4 March <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/liu-zhiyuan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/liu-zhiyuan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Liu Zhiyuan</span><span class="tp">895–948</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-the-pious"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-the-pious.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George the Pious</span><span class="tp">1484–1543</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antonio-vivaldi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonio-vivaldi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antonio Vivaldi</span><span class="tp">1678–1741</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muhammad-ali-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</span><span class="tp">1769–1849</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mihaly-karolyi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mihaly-karolyi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mihály Károlyi</span><span class="tp">1875–1955</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-carrero-blanco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luis-carrero-blanco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luis Carrero Blanco</span><span class="tp">1904–1973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tancredo-neves"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tancredo-neves.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tancredo Neves</span><span class="tp">1910–1985</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 4 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/saladin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/saladin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Saladin</span><span class="tp">d. 1193</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-of-vladimir"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yuri-ii-of-vladimir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yuri II of Vladimir</span><span class="tp">1189–1238</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-archduke-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sigismund, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="tp">1427–1496</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fausto-sozzini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fausto-sozzini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fausto Sozzini</span><span class="tp">1539–1604</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/franz-marc"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/franz-marc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Franz Marc</span><span class="tp">1880–1916</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/javier-perez-de-cuellar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/javier-perez-de-cuellar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Javier Pérez de Cuéllar</span><span class="tp">1920–2020</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
